KG42.register("nodes-43bd532884244aeeea8fc606",{"id":"COMP-dddaa2edb4acd670","code":"SET018","label":"Electricity-sharing settlement, service-fee allocation and regional revenue-cost accounting","definition":"Includes distinct monetary outputs: the electrical-energy charge or revenue term Pr_i^h(x_i^h−P_i^h); the total ESP service fee S=βΣ_{h=1}^{H}min(TSP^h,TBP^h); and the individual service-fee share S_i^h=β|NP_i^h|min(TSP^h,TBP^h)/(TSP^h+TBP^h). Also retains the regional revenue-and-expenditure constraint TBP·Pr_buy=TSP·Pr_sell+(TBP−TSP)λ^{buy} when 0≤SDR≤1.","layer":"L8","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"settlement.payment","concept_ids":["settlement.payment"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: prosumer electrical-energy revenues and expenditures, ESP service-fee revenue, and individual allocation","Electrical-energy billing operation and output: multiply the applicable electricity price by the difference between adjusted consumption and PV production to obtain a monetary charge or revenue term","Service-fee operation and output: compute the total S from the shared quantity, and compute the share S_i^h from the net-quantity contribution","Revenue-and-expenditure relation: electricity-purchase payments cover internal electricity-sale revenue and the grid purchase cost of residual demand"]},"exclusions":["The ESP is responsible for fee collection and regional payment balance","β is the shared-energy service-fee coefficient, and no specific value is given","The total service fee is accumulated over the H periods of the operating day, and individual shares are computed by i and h","The service fee should cover shared losses and organizational expenditure","Pr_i^h(x_i^h−P_i^h) is only a monetary term; the inconvenience-cost term belongs to the entity scheduling-cost model"],"members":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"Updated requested net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h ≥ 0, which contribute to total buying power. Updated offered net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h \u003c 0, whose magnitudes contribute to total selling power. The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. Final internal prices are decided when the price-coordination process reaches a state in which no PV prosumer can adjust its schedule further. Scope: Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. Condition: After sufficient iterations, all PV prosumers can no longer adjust their schedules in response to the internal prices. The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1. Internal prices must remain between the feed-in tariff and the utility-grid electricity purchase price. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Internal-price design must guarantee the economic balance of the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. The internal selling price is Pr^{h}_{sell} = (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}). Scope: Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR^h ≤ 1. Both internal buying and selling prices equal the utility-grid export tariff. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. Condition: SDR > 1. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_sell^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h \u003c 0. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_buy^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h ≥ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"56caf15ff85b7048a35707f2567847b37f3ebab30e4076668d222d792bbea136","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","node_id":"settlement.payment","function":"settlement.payment","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h. The service fee is directly proportional to the amount of shared local PV energy. Scope: The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. Each prosumer's service-fee share is allocated according to its contribution of shared local energy. Scope: Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. The service fee should cover sharing-power losses and other possible expenditures for organizing sharing activities. Scope: Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"fe990a393f5f5a128c4aeb63d22e38523e42ffec212540ef5888171d9331c382","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008","node_id":"settlement.payment","function":"settlement.payment","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true}],"paper_ids":["06-sdr_energy_sharing"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"der When SDR = 0, which means no PV prosumer sells power, ded the required energy is bought from the","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34).","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net powe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In the energy sharing zone, self-consumption of PV energy is still the first choice for PV prosumers. If PV energy can not satisfy the load demand, the PV prosumer would purchase energy agented by the ESP. If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP. In order to keep the fairness of energy sharing, the ESP should not have an optimal objective with any tendency, but it still needs to charge for service fee with the prosumers, as to cover the power losses and other possible expenditures.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"In the energy sharing zone, self-consumption of PV energy is still the first choice for PV prosumers. If PV energy can not satisfy the load demand, the PV prosumer would purchase energy agented by the ESP. If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP. In order to keep the fairness of energy sharing, the ESP should not have an optimal objective with any tendency, but it still needs to charge for service fee with the prosumers, as to cover the power losses and other possible expenditures."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-19","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the service fee from the participating prosumers, which is directly proportional to the amount of shared PV energy. The income of the ESP in an operation day is deﬁned:\nS = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right) \\quad (20)\nwhere \\beta is the charged percentage of shared energy.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the service fee from the participating prosumers, which is directly proportional to the amount of shared PV energy. The income of the ESP in an operation day is deﬁned:\nS = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right) \\quad (20)\nwhere \\beta is the charged percentage of shared energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"h=1 where inci is the equivalent inconvenience cost of PV prosumer i, αi is the sensitivity coefﬁcie","equation_id":"(14),(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-20","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"First, we think it is fair for all the prosumers to pay for the service fees according to their contributions of shared energy. The service fee distribution model can be formulated as:\nS_{i}^{h} = \\frac{\\beta \\cdot \\left| NP_{i}^{h} \\right| \\cdot \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right)}{TSP^{h} + TBP^{h}} \\quad (21)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"First, we think it is fair for all the prosumers to pay for the service fees according to their contributions of shared energy. The service fee distribution model can be formulated as:\nS_{i}^{h} = \\frac{\\beta \\cdot \\left| NP_{i}^{h} \\right| \\cdot \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right)}{TSP^{h} + TBP^{h}} \\quad (21)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-39","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"t β · NP ih · min TSP h, TBP h (21) Shi = TSP h + TBP h ⎨ Moreover, for the value of β, the service ","equation_id":"(20)-(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Moreover, for the value of \\beta, the service fee should cover the losses of sharing power and other possible expenditures for organizing the sharing activities. In fact, the ESP is a virtual entity that cannot produce any PV energy, and thus the proﬁt should be limited for actual applications.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Moreover, for the value of \\beta, the service fee should cover the losses of sharing power and other possible expenditures for organizing the sharing activities. In fact, the ESP is a virtual entity that cannot produce any PV energy, and thus the proﬁt should be limited for actual applications."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34).","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["energy_payment_and_service_fee_allocation"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L8-68ff6e174c","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L8","ontological_kind":"composite_rule"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"settlement.payment","source_occurrences":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"Updated requested net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h ≥ 0, which contribute to total buying power. Updated offered net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h \u003c 0, whose magnitudes contribute to total selling power. The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. Final internal prices are decided when the price-coordination process reaches a state in which no PV prosumer can adjust its schedule further. Scope: Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. Condition: After sufficient iterations, all PV prosumers can no longer adjust their schedules in response to the internal prices. The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1. Internal prices must remain between the feed-in tariff and the utility-grid electricity purchase price. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Internal-price design must guarantee the economic balance of the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. The internal selling price is Pr^{h}_{sell} = (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}). Scope: Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR^h ≤ 1. Both internal buying and selling prices equal the utility-grid export tariff. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. Condition: SDR > 1. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_sell^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h \u003c 0. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_buy^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h ≥ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"56caf15ff85b7048a35707f2567847b37f3ebab30e4076668d222d792bbea136"},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::settlement.payment","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h. The service fee is directly proportional to the amount of shared local PV energy. Scope: The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. Each prosumer's service-fee share is allocated according to its contribution of shared local energy. Scope: Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. The service fee should cover sharing-power losses and other possible expenditures for organizing sharing activities. Scope: Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"fe990a393f5f5a128c4aeb63d22e38523e42ffec212540ef5888171d9331c382"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E18"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"der When SDR = 0, which means no PV prosumer sells power, ded the required energy is bought from the","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g02-E-19"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e05","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net powe","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"In the energy sharing zone, self-consumption of PV energy is still the first choice for PV prosumers. If PV energy can not satisfy the load demand, the PV prosumer would purchase energy agented by the ESP. If the demand of the PV prosumer is less than the production of PV source, the redundant PV power will be shared with other PV prosumers or sold to the utility grid via the ESP. In order to keep the fairness of energy sharing, the ESP should not have an optimal objective with any tendency, but it still needs to charge for service fee with the prosumers, as to cover the power losses and other possible expenditures."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-19","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the service fee from the participating prosumers, which is directly proportional to the amount of shared PV energy. The income of the ESP in an operation day is deﬁned:\nS = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right) \\quad (20)\nwhere \\beta is the charged percentage of shared energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","expression":"Pr_i^{h} \\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h} \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"h=1 where inci is the equivalent inconvenience cost of PV prosumer i, αi is the sensitivity coefﬁcie","equation_id":"(14),(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The service fee is directly proportional to the amount of shared local PV energy. Scope: The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid.","expression":"S = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R008-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-19"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-19","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(20)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the service fee from the participating prosumers, which is directly proportional to the amount of shared PV energy. The income of the ESP in an operation day is deﬁned:\nS = \\beta \\sum_{h=1}^{H} \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right) \\quad (20)\nwhere \\beta is the charged percentage of shared energy."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Each prosumer's service-fee share is allocated according to its contribution of shared local energy. Scope: Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers.","expression":"S_{i}^{h} = \\frac{\\beta \\cdot \\left| NP_{i}^{h} \\right| \\cdot \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right)}{TSP^{h} + TBP^{h}}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["product.local_energy","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R008-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-20"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-20","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"tr ri D. Income Model of the ESP pr As the agent of PV energy sharing, the ESP could charge the w se","equation_id":"(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"First, we think it is fair for all the prosumers to pay for the service fees according to their contributions of shared energy. The service fee distribution model can be formulated as:\nS_{i}^{h} = \\frac{\\beta \\cdot \\left| NP_{i}^{h} \\right| \\cdot \\min \\left( TSP^{h}, TBP^{h} \\right)}{TSP^{h} + TBP^{h}} \\quad (21)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The service fee should cover sharing-power losses and other possible expenditures for organizing sharing activities. Scope: Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R008-theta-beta"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-39"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-39","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p06-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":"D. Income Model of the ESP","anchor_text":"t β · NP ih · min TSP h, TBP h (21) Shi = TSP h + TBP h ⎨ Moreover, for the value of β, the service ","equation_id":"(20)-(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Moreover, for the value of \\beta, the service fee should cover the losses of sharing power and other possible expenditures for organizing the sharing activities. In fact, the ESP is a virtual entity that cannot produce any PV energy, and thus the proﬁt should be limited for actual applications."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, the energy-sharing zone's economic-balance condition equates total buying payments with internal selling receipts plus the ESP's utility-grid purchase cost of the residual: TBP·Pr_buy = TSP·Pr_sell + (TBP−TSP)λ^buy.","expression":"TBP \\cdot Pr_{buy} = TSP \\cdot Pr_{sell} + (TBP - TSP)\\lambda^{buy}, \\quad 0 \\leq SDR \\leq 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-e04","v141-b-g03-E18"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R008-theta-beta","symbol":"\\beta","meaning":"Charged percentage of shared energy, i.e. the service-fee rate applied to the actually shared (matched) local PV energy in the ESP's aggregate service income.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"β"},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g01-e02","v141-b-g02-E-39"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::theta::v141-c-R008-theta-beta"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::settlement.payment","stage":"L8","subtype":"energy_payment_and_service_fee_allocation","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"Includes distinct monetary outputs: the electrical-energy charge or revenue term Pr_i^h(x_i^h−P_i^h); the total ESP service fee S=βΣ_{h=1}^{H}min(TSP^h,TBP^h); and the individual service-fee share S_i^h=β|NP_i^h|min(TSP^h,TBP^h)/(TSP^h+TBP^h). Also retains the regional revenue-and-expenditure constraint TBP·Pr_buy=TSP·Pr_sell+(TBP−TSP)λ^{buy} when 0≤SDR≤1.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: prosumer electrical-energy revenues and expenditures, ESP service-fee revenue, and individual allocation","Electrical-energy billing operation and output: multiply the applicable electricity price by the difference between adjusted consumption and PV production to obtain a monetary charge or revenue term","Service-fee operation and output: compute the total S from the shared quantity, and compute the share S_i^h from the net-quantity contribution","Revenue-and-expenditure relation: electricity-purchase payments cover internal electricity-sale revenue and the grid purchase cost of residual demand"],"variation_fields":["The ESP is responsible for fee collection and regional payment balance","β is the shared-energy service-fee coefficient, and no specific value is given","The total service fee is accumulated over the H periods of the operating day, and individual shares are computed by i and h","The service fee should cover shared losses and organizational expenditure","Pr_i^h(x_i^h−P_i^h) is only a monetary term; the inconvenience-cost term belongs to the entity scheduling-cost model"],"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"settlement.payment","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/266"});
